Changes to the original Python source for AmigaPython
-------------------------------------------------------

This file historically described diffs against stock Python **1.6**.
AmigaPython is now based on **Python 2.7.18**.  Keep the classic notes
below as a record of the original port techniques; prefer the current
Source/ tree, vmakefile / SMAKEFILE, and project VCS history for what
actually ships in 2.7.18.


AmigaPython 2.7.18 (amigazen project) — summary
-----------------------------------------------

- Interpreter / library updated from the classic 2.0 Amiga line to final
  Python 2.7.18 (Include/patchlevel.h VERSION "2.7.18").
- Primary build path: VBCC + PosixLib (vmakefile → Python27).  SAS/C
  SMAKEFILE retained as a legacy path (Python27_sas).
- Builtin `amiga` module: expanded POSIX surface; Doslib helpers,
  ArgParser / constants via _amiga_dos; to_unix / from_unix; ASL
  FileRequest / MessageBox; locale OpenCatalog; icon DiskObject.
- ARexx as `_arexx` / `arexx`; I-Net225 remains unsupported; networking
  via bsdsocket.library.
- Amiga docs: Amiga_Misc/Docs and Python/docs/amiga updated for 2.7.18.


Classic notes (against original 1.6 source)
-------------------------------------------

General:

At different places Amiga-specific code was added, removed or changed,
typically gated with preprocessor symbols:
_AMIGA : Defined when compiling on Amiga.
         Indicates Amiga specific code.
__SASC : Defined when compiling with the SAS/C compiler.
         Indicates SAS/C specific code.
AMITCP : Defined when using AmiTCP / bsdsocket-style networking.
INET225: Defined when using INET-225 (no longer supported).


Added subdir Amiga_Misc with:
	README                  - describing text
	mkdiffs.py              - makes diffs against original distribution
	Diffs/                  - output dir for mkdiff.py
	DISCL_and_COPYRIGHT     - disclaimer & historic copyright text
	testset/                - additional tests for Amiga modules
	unused/                 - currently unused stuff
	Docs/                   - Amiga docs for distribution
	experimental_modules/   - exploratory extensions


- Supplied custom makefile for Amiga's SAS/C: SMAKEFILE.
  Supplied SAS/C compiler options file: SCOPTIONS.
  (Later: SMAKEFILE split per main directory; VBCC vmakefile added for 2.7.18)

- Added Prototype files for many source files (SAS/C era).
  See `protos' directories in: Modules, Objects, Parser, Python.

- Created / maintained Amiga config and modules:
	Include/pyconfig.h (and historic config.h)
	Include/osdefs.h Amiga defines
	Modules/config.c
	Modules/environment related code
	Modules/amiga/amigamodule.c (and related amiga_*.c)
	Modules/ARexxmodule.c / _arexx
	Modules/Doslibmodule.c (APIs now also on amiga)


Include/Python.h:
	- Amiga / SAS/C includes as required by the toolchain

Include/osdefs.h:
	- AMIGA specific #defines; VERSION string for the port

Parser/intrcheck.c:
	- SAS/C specific ^C handling (classic)

Objects/longobject.c:
	- sizeof workarounds for SAS/C where needed

Python/sigcheck.c:
	- stack checking code

Python/sysmodule.c:
	- absolute path check in PySys_SetArgv

Python/import.c:
	- path building via dos.library/AddPart (classic)
	- case-sensitive import check (PYTHONCASEOK to relax)

Python/pythonrun.c:
	- filename match behaviour for .pyc / .pyo on Amiga


Modules/mathmodule.c:
	- SAS/C direct math call macros (classic)

Modules/getbuildinfo.c:
	- Amiga version string ($VER)

Modules/timemodule.c:
	- floatsleep() (uses select() when available)

Modules/getpath.c:
	- Amiga PYTHONPATH / executable path / assign handling

Modules/cryptmodule.c, grpmodule.c, pwdmodule.c, syslogmodule.c:
	- AmiTCP / usergroup includes and adaptations

Modules/socketmodule.c:
	- AmiTCP / bsdsocket includes and API shims
	- IoctlSocket for setblocking, etc.

Modules/main.c / Embed/AmigaPythonEmbed.c:
	- AmiTCP init & cleanup; Workbench / assign startup pieces

Modules/selectmodule.c:
	- optional 5th AmigaDOS signal-mask argument


- Lib/plat-amiga and site-python / Amiga path modules
- Lib/lib-dynload directory historically for exec_prefix behaviour
- Library tweaks: os.py, tempfile.py, posixpath stub, amigapath,
  site.py, Amiga-aware tests


Unicode (classic 1.6/2.0 era notes; 2.7.18 uses stock Unicode with
Amiga build options as configured):

Modules/unicodedata / database loading may still use Amiga-specific
strategies depending on toolchain limits — see Modules/amiga and
pyconfig.h for the active build.


NON-AMIGA trees historically held unused upstream files omitted from
Aminet source archives for space.
